    <decisions>
        <description>Nothing can be synced until the subscription points at a renewal opportunity. That lookup is maintained by &quot;Subscription - Set Renewal Opportunity&quot;.</description>
        <name>Has_Renewal_Opportunity</name>
        <label>Has Renewal Opportunity?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Nothing to Sync</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Renewal_Opp_Set</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Subscription.Ruby__RenewalOpportunity__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Renewal_Opportunity</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Renewal Opp Set</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Opportunity subscriptions on a closed opportunity record what was actually booked. They are never created, updated or deleted here. A closed opportunity still stamped on the subscription means no open renewal exists yet, and there is nothing to sync.</description>
        <name>Is_Renewal_Opportunity_Open</name>
        <label>Is Renewal Opportunity Open?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Closed - Leave Booked History Alone</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Open</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Renewal_Opportunity.IsClosed</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Is_Term_Aligned</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Open</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Only rows on opportunities that are still open are stranded. Rows on closed opportunities are booked history and stay.</description>
        <name>Is_Stranded_Opportunity_Open</name>
        <label>Is Stranded Opportunity Open?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Loop_Stranded_Opportunity_Subscriptions</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Closed - Leave Booked History Alone</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Stranded_Open</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Loop_Stranded_Opportunity_Subscriptions.null__NotFound</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Add_Stranded_Opportunity_Subscription</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Stranded Open</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>The row belongs only on the opportunity that renews this subscription&apos;s own term. The renewal opportunity must start within 14 days of the day after the subscription ends. An early renewal moves one subscription&apos;s boundary and leaves a lapsed or unrenewed sibling behind; without this test that sibling rides along and inflates the baseline. A blank service start date allows the row, so a missing date never silently drops one.</description>
        <name>Is_Term_Aligned</name>
        <label>Is Term Aligned?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Opportunity_Subscription_to_Remove</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Not This Subscription&apos;s Renewal</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Aligned</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>isTermAligned</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Should_Row_Exist</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Aligned</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Active and Ended subscriptions keep their opportunity subscription. Ended means the term lapsed, and the renewal is often closed late, so the baseline must survive. Cancelled, ScheduledForCancel and Draft contribute no baseline and have their row removed.</description>
        <name>Should_Row_Exist</name>
        <label>Should Row Exist?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Opportunity_Subscription_to_Remove</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - Remove</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Active_or_Ended</name>
            <conditionLogic>1 OR 2</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Subscription.Ruby__Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Active</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Subscription.Ruby__Status__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Ended</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Opportunity_Subscription</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Active or Ended</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>True when this renewal opportunity renews this subscription&apos;s own term. Compares the opportunity service start date with the day after the subscription ends, and allows 14 days of slack for a late renewal. True as well when either date is blank, so a missing date never deletes a row.</description>
        <name>isTermAligned</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>ISBLANK({!Get_Renewal_Opportunity.Service_Start_Date__c}) || ISBLANK({!Get_Subscription.Ruby__SubscriptionEndDate__c}) || ABS({!Get_Renewal_Opportunity.Service_Start_Date__c} - ({!Get_Subscription.Ruby__SubscriptionEndDate__c} + 1)) &lt;= 14</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Subscription - After Update - Update Opportunity Subscriptions {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Subscription - After Update - Update Opportunity Subscriptions</label>
    <loops>
        <name>Loop_Stranded_Opportunity_Subscriptions</name>
        <label>Loop Stranded Opportunity Subscriptions</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <collectionReference>Get_Stranded_Opportunity_Subscriptions</collectionReference>
        <iterationOrder>Asc</iterationOrder>
        <nextValueConnector>
            <targetReference>Is_Stranded_Opportunity_Open</targetReference>
        </nextValueConnector>
        <noMoreValuesConnector>
            <targetReference>Any_Stranded_Rows</targetReference>
        </noMoreValuesConnector>
    </loops>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordCreates>
